{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01132",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.01,
      "end_seconds": 4.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.78,
      "end_seconds": 8.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.28,
      "end_seconds": 15.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Um, so... a blocked ear. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.92,
      "end_seconds": 18.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.37,
      "end_seconds": 22.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "About... well, two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.54,
      "end_seconds": 33.46,
      "duration_seconds": 9.92,
      "text": "Right, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.21,
      "end_seconds": 42.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "A eight out of ten, I suppose. It's worse with showering."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.39,
      "end_seconds": 48.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.88,
      "end_seconds": 64.1,
      "duration_seconds": 14.22,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get muffled hearing on one side as well. The, The muffled hearing on one side? That's been for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.98,
      "end_seconds": 72.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.31,
      "end_seconds": 85.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.87,
      "end_seconds": 102.9,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 116 over 71, pulse is 79 beats a minute, temperature 36.8."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.55,
      "end_seconds": 106.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.5,
      "end_seconds": 110.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.8,
      "end_seconds": 116.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.79,
      "end_seconds": 120.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.59,
      "end_seconds": 124.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.49,
      "end_seconds": 135.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "There's a lot of wax blocking the right ear canal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.72,
      "end_seconds": 143.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. A few quick ones: discharge, dizziness, ear pain or ringing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.79,
      "end_seconds": 147.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.96,
      "end_seconds": 153.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.85,
      "end_seconds": 157.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "No, uh, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.76,
      "end_seconds": 170.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.52,
      "end_seconds": 181.91,
      "duration_seconds": 10.39,
      "text": "Erm, I had a reaction to erythromycin when I was younger, a rash, and I've avoided it since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.28,
      "end_seconds": 196.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.23,
      "end_seconds": 201.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.19,
      "end_seconds": 205.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.02,
      "end_seconds": 209.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.51,
      "end_seconds": 214.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Okay, what does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.72,
      "end_seconds": 220.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.54,
      "end_seconds": 223.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.42,
      "end_seconds": 229.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "I had part of my thyroid removed years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.0,
      "end_seconds": 233.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.52,
      "end_seconds": 239.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "I've had epilepsy for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.05,
      "end_seconds": 240.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.45,
      "end_seconds": 257.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.38,
      "end_seconds": 269.52,
      "duration_seconds": 11.14,
      "text": "I take sodium valproate, 500 milligrams, twice a day. Sorry, what was I saying, I take olive oil drops, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.54,
      "end_seconds": 276.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. This looks most like earwax blocking the ear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.1,
      "end_seconds": 280.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.8,
      "end_seconds": 302.56,
      "duration_seconds": 20.76,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's earwax blocking the ear, and we'll know more once the ear irrigation is back. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had a blocked ear for two days, and no dizziness or discharge."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.35,
      "end_seconds": 304.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.86,
      "end_seconds": 326.94,
      "duration_seconds": 20.08,
      "text": "I'm going to order ear irrigation, for wax. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. Use the olive oil drops for a week and then we'll syringe the ear. See me again in one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.0,
      "end_seconds": 331.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Uh, I'll note it in my calendar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.99,
      "end_seconds": 337.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 339.04,
      "end_seconds": 343.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "So, you know, thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.73,
      "end_seconds": 344.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}